    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d373">

                <pb facs="0513" n="409" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg409"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 837.911/19.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-20">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 20, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Delay in prosecution is rapidly convincing newspapers that our attitude was mere
                    bluff and that nothing will be done. Several papers publish sneering articles
                    which, although they avoid personalities, are most insulting to the good faith
                    of our Government from which, the newspapers intimate, they have nothing to
                    fear.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
